  "starterCode": "import torch\n\ndef inference_multi_head_latent_attention(x: list, W_dkv: list, W_uk: list, W_uv: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Implement Multi-Head Latent Attention (MLA)** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport torch\n\ndef inference_multi_head_latent_attention(x: list, W_dkv: list, W_uk: list, W_uv: list) -> dict:\n    tx, wdkv, wuk, wuv = torch.tensor(x, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(W_dkv, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(W_uk, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(W_uv, dtype=torch.float32)\n    ckv = torch.matmul(tx, wdkv)\n    return {'compressed_latent': torch.round(ckv, decimals=4).tolist(), 'decompressed_keys': torch.round(torch.matmul(ckv, wuk), decimals=4).tolist(), 'decompressed_values': torch.round(torch.matmul(ckv, wuv), decimals=4).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
